About DemoSpriteDemoSprite demonstrates a MacApp control with smooth animation implementedusing the QuickTimeª sprite toolbox. The MakeSpriteControl application has a bunch of pictures of a knob and an'acur' resource that specifies the 'PICT' resource IDs. It creates a resourcefile with a 'sprt' resource that contains all the pictures in compressed form. The pictures are compressed with a codec that makes their background colortransparent. The background color and the 'acur' resource ID are hard-coded,but they are easy to change in MakeSpriteControl.cp. The DemoSprite application is DemoDialogs plus a new Sprite Control window. TSpriteControl is a subclass of TControl that reads in the 'sprt' resourcefor its resource ID. It creates a sprite world with a single sprite in it. The control value is the same as the sprite's current image index. TSpriteControl uses the same view template as TPicture. To add a spritecontrol to a window, add a picture and change the class name and theevent number. TKnobControl is a subclass of TSpriteControl that sets the control value basedon the angle of the mouse relative to the knob. DemoSprite was built with QuickTime 3.0b7. Tom BeckerApple Computer, Inc.